# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lovable Cloud project exports — NEVER COMMIT
# These contain personal data (user emails, profiles) and bcrypt password
# hashes from auth.users. Inspect schema only; never print row data.
# Patterns are deliberately broad because the exact filename Lovable emits
# has not been confirmed — widen further rather than risk a commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*export*.sql
*export*.sql.gz
*export*.zip
*export*.tar
*export*.tar.gz
*export*.dump
*export*.backup
lovable-export*/
bidintel-export*/
supabase-export*/
*.pgdump
*.dump

# Terraform working directories and local state.
#
# .terraform/ holds provider binaries — the AWS provider alone is 760 MB, well
# over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, which is how this was noticed.
#
# *.tfplan is a saved binary plan. It is a point-in-time snapshot of intended
# changes that can contain resource attributes marked sensitive, and it is
# meaningless to anyone else's working directory.
#
# terraform.tfstate* — real state lives in S3 (bidintel-tfstate-008041477140).
# The only local state files are leftovers from phase 1's bootstrap, before the
# backend existed, and state routinely contains secrets in plaintext.
#
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored: provider version pinning
# belongs in version control.
.terraform/
*.tfplan
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.*
terraform.tfstate.backup
